WEBVTT

00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:31.239
Are you awake?

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.662
Don't worry. I won't suck your blood.

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:41.624
My name is Elisha. What's yours?

00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:45.086
Momo.

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:49.716
Where's Fine? Where is my friend?

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:50.717
She's fine.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.470
Where? Where is she?

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:56.681
Don't be hasty.
I can show you where later.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.933
But first, eat this.

00:01:02.812 --> 00:01:04.230
You were lucky.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:08.526
<i>It was by chance</i>
<i>that we stumbled upon you.</i>

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:16.659
This is delicious.

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.539
It looks like they like you, Momo.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:28.004
Watch out below.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.396
-There's electricity?
-Yes.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:50.068
As a result, we have no shortage
of food or blood here.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:55.031
So we don't have to fight
and can live peacefully together.

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:22.892
You really are living in harmony.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.811
You believe it now, don't you?

00:02:24.894 --> 00:02:26.771
That this place is a paradise.

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:30.650
So please don't look so sullen.
Show me your smile.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.745
Come with me. Your friend is this way.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.469
Are you feeling all right?
Perhaps we should try…

00:02:58.553 --> 00:02:59.804
Please keep resting.

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:03.016
Shut up. I can't sit around in this place.

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:05.518
No, you mustn't open that.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.897
You still aren't fully recovered.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:09.856
Fine!

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:12.734
Elisha, good timing.

00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:14.527
Momo. You're all right?

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:17.614
Yes. You're looking a lot better too.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.992
This is Elisha. She helped us.

00:03:22.952 --> 00:03:25.288
Is that right? You have my gratitude.

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.917
Look, Fine, we made it.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.919
The place we were looking for.

00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:32.211
This place?

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:38.885
Please, let me out of here.
I can't do this anymore,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.346
being connected to these tubes
and having my blood drained.

00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:42.805
Keep your hands off of her.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.934
How did you manage to come out this far?

00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.144
Beware! You should watch out.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.104
-Protect your friend!
-Please, wait outside.

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.649
-There now. Calm down.
-Let go! Don't do this!

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.945
Sorry about that. That was a vampire
that we'd taken in recently.

00:03:57.028 --> 00:03:59.489
-He has a blood disease.
-A blood disease?

00:04:00.114 --> 00:04:02.408
I'm sorry you had to see that.

00:04:03.117 --> 00:04:05.578
-You must be elated, Elisha.
-What?

00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:07.330
You've been saying for the longest time

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:10.166
that you wanted a friend
around the same age as you.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.919
I told you not to tell anyone.

00:04:20.343 --> 00:04:22.595
that you want a friend
around the same age as you.

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:24.597
What's with this eerie-looking ship?

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.100
I've never read anything about this place.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:29.352
Hello.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:33.648
Plus, that guy from earlier seemed like
he was held against his will.

00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:35.858
I'm sure you're overthinking it.

00:04:39.487 --> 00:04:42.573
Hey! Come over here!

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:52.166
I told you,
I've never seen a map like that.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.627
I only gave them a place for the night.

00:04:54.711 --> 00:04:58.631
Now leave me alone.
I want nothing to do with humans.

00:04:59.215 --> 00:05:02.302
I've seen cards like this
being passed around before.

00:05:02.385 --> 00:05:04.012
Do you recognize this place?

00:05:04.095 --> 00:05:06.806
I believe it's somewhere
in the ice lands up north.

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:08.391
But that area is vast.

00:05:09.183 --> 00:05:11.728
-It's Volskaya.
-What?

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.355
It's a village
located in a permafrost region.

00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:16.983
I've seen this church
in our research material.

00:05:17.066 --> 00:05:21.237
A submarine washed up, causing
massive environmental contamination.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.656
The native villages have all perished.

00:05:24.574 --> 00:05:26.617
How do you know about this?

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:30.204
Any scientist would know about this.
Let's get going.

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:31.622
Boss.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.459
You have a call from Central.

00:05:48.056 --> 00:05:49.474
There we go.

00:05:49.557 --> 00:05:52.810
You can add more wood yourselves
if it's not hot enough.

00:05:52.894 --> 00:05:54.270
Thank you.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.486
This feels great, doesn't it?

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.448
Momo. Take this.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:09.786
Protect yourself with this
if anything happens.

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.745
What?

00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:14.332
We'll see for ourselves

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:18.336
whether this is really the place
that we've been looking for.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:21.547
Yeah.

00:06:23.466 --> 00:06:25.551
Could you hold onto that, Fine?

00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:31.265
Where are you going?

00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:33.476
I'm taking a cold plunge. You should come.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.854
Really? I don't do too well with those.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.481
I know.

00:06:44.862 --> 00:06:49.784
To this day, vampires and humans on
the outside are unable to cease fighting.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:57.708
I'm grateful that the art and music
that we've created guided you here.

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:00.294
Welcome to our village.

00:07:04.132 --> 00:07:09.262
I've traveled from Central with hopes
of finding a better place like this.

00:07:10.346 --> 00:07:14.016
If there's any way I can contribute
around here, please let me be of service.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.311
You're next, Fine.

00:07:20.648 --> 00:07:22.024
Thanks for having us.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.239
All right, everyone.
Let's get things started.

00:07:45.173 --> 00:07:47.341
Momo, come dance with me.

00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:52.638
-Go on. Dance.
-Now, come with me.

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:56.684
Like this.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.478
And then jump.

00:07:59.103 --> 00:08:00.062
Then do this.

00:08:00.563 --> 00:08:01.397
Now together.

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:46.484
Momo!

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.196
We're officially friends now.

00:08:50.279 --> 00:08:52.657
Let's stay like this forever.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.410
Yeah. Thank you.

00:09:25.982 --> 00:09:26.899
Fine.

00:09:27.942 --> 00:09:29.068
Thank you.

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:31.862
For what?

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:35.324
I feel so happy right now.

00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:40.162
I can't believe there are
this many people that love music.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.164
Back in my town,

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:45.126
singing and dancing
was strictly prohibited.

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:49.714
But the people here are so free.

00:09:50.298 --> 00:09:53.509
So thank you, Fine.

00:09:54.176 --> 00:09:55.761
For bringing me here.

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.016
Freedom, huh?

00:10:04.145 --> 00:10:06.439
-Momo, you--
-Momo!

00:10:07.023 --> 00:10:09.191
We're about to start up again.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:10.318
Okay!

00:10:14.155 --> 00:10:17.199
Fine, what's wrong?

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.539
Nothing. I need some air. You go ahead.

00:10:24.206 --> 00:10:26.417
Okay. I'll be waiting for you.

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:31.464
Here. Come on.
Everyone can't wait for you to come back.

00:10:37.595 --> 00:10:39.555
You've managed to travel quite far.

00:10:40.598 --> 00:10:43.309
Allegro, how are you here?

00:10:46.354 --> 00:10:47.938
This makes me think of old times.

00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:53.486
Remember when we used to sneak out
of town together when we were kids?

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:56.072
We went searching for places like this.

00:11:00.868 --> 00:11:04.038
Fine, let's go home.
You can't keep pushing yourself.

00:11:05.122 --> 00:11:06.791
Your body won't hold up much longer.

00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:10.878
Don't confuse your past
with that Warm girl.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.714
Can't you hear?

00:11:15.216 --> 00:11:18.386
She seems to be doing fine without you.

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:25.768
I'll be there for you
if you can't bear it on your own.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:28.938
<i>If my being here</i>

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:33.317
will get in the way
of her happiness, then…

00:11:38.697 --> 00:11:41.659
Fine, come home with me.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.049
I hope you're not feeling sorry for Momo

00:11:57.133 --> 00:11:59.427
and you haven't been
letting her get away on purpose.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.263
She's been hard to handle.
Just like her mother.

00:12:02.847 --> 00:12:04.181
How far is it from here?

00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:07.393
Going across the lake
should take about six hours.

00:12:09.353 --> 00:12:10.229
That stinks!

00:12:10.729 --> 00:12:12.940
Stop smoking. It's evil.

00:12:13.524 --> 00:12:17.319
It's hard to believe
you've chased after her this far.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:20.239
Do you think you understand
how this feels for a mother?

00:12:20.781 --> 00:12:21.740
Let's go.

00:12:22.283 --> 00:12:23.159
"For a mother"?

00:12:24.118 --> 00:12:26.745
Aren't you just desperate
to maintain your status?

00:12:27.371 --> 00:12:30.207
If Momo died, the guys at Central
would get off your case.

00:12:30.791 --> 00:12:34.587
You'd have a chance at maintaining
your authority if that happens, right?

00:12:36.255 --> 00:12:38.757
Our country has no use for traitors.

00:12:39.633 --> 00:12:42.595
If you choose to disobey,
you have to deal with the consequences.

00:13:09.872 --> 00:13:10.873
Fine?

00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:25.137
<i>Use this if something ever happens.</i>

00:13:28.849 --> 00:13:30.893
Momo, what's wrong?

00:13:31.644 --> 00:13:33.229
-Fine has left.
-What?

00:13:33.312 --> 00:13:34.355
That's horrible.

00:13:36.398 --> 00:13:38.984
-I have to go find her.
-Calm down, Momo.

00:13:39.068 --> 00:13:41.612
Leave it to us. We'll find her.

00:13:41.695 --> 00:13:43.572
-But…
-It's all right.

00:13:43.656 --> 00:13:46.283
I'm sure we'll find her in no time.
Wait here.

00:13:46.367 --> 00:13:50.079
There are lakes that are starting to melt
all over this region.

00:13:50.162 --> 00:13:51.580
-It's very dangerous.
-Wait!

00:13:51.664 --> 00:13:54.166
-Please protect her.
-Leave it to me.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.501
Elisha!

00:13:55.584 --> 00:13:57.586
-Let's go.
-Be quick.

00:13:58.629 --> 00:14:01.173
Please, let me help too!

00:14:02.424 --> 00:14:05.511
Hurry. There will be a storm
in the east this afternoon.

00:14:05.594 --> 00:14:07.304
Move quick. Head west.

00:14:07.388 --> 00:14:08.764
We're using valuable energy.

00:14:08.847 --> 00:14:10.391
Be sure not to lose them.

00:14:15.771 --> 00:14:18.065
I have to get out of here somehow.

00:14:31.829 --> 00:14:33.038
You should lie down.

00:14:33.122 --> 00:14:34.874
You don't have enough blood in you.

00:14:35.708 --> 00:14:39.086
Wait here. I'll call for backup.

00:14:43.215 --> 00:14:46.594
That postcard claimed
that this is a paradise.

00:14:47.177 --> 00:14:49.805
A place where humans and vampires coexist.

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:52.558
Careful not to develop
any compassion for them.

00:14:53.851 --> 00:14:55.895
I'm a different person
than I was back then.

00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:58.314
I'm not some 15-year-old punk anymore.

00:14:59.356 --> 00:15:00.441
I hope that's true.

00:15:01.233 --> 00:15:03.569
<i>This paradise isn't real.</i>

00:15:03.652 --> 00:15:06.196
<i>I can't say exactly</i>
<i>what tactics they're using to cover it up,</i>

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:09.033
<i>but I'm positive it's all deception.</i>

00:15:17.708 --> 00:15:19.418
Hey. Oh, no.

00:15:23.839 --> 00:15:24.715
Fine.

00:15:35.225 --> 00:15:37.645
Momo, please stop.

00:15:37.728 --> 00:15:39.355
If not, I'll have to shoot.

00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:43.150
Crap.

00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.750
What did I tell you?

00:15:59.833 --> 00:16:01.877
You were supposed to keep her locked up.

00:16:24.274 --> 00:16:26.694
-Crap.
-Ambush her from above.

00:16:26.777 --> 00:16:27.903
Okay.

00:16:45.129 --> 00:16:46.588
Look below you.

00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:48.424
You can see the duct, right?

00:16:48.966 --> 00:16:50.342
Get inside from there.

00:16:51.719 --> 00:16:52.636
Hurry.

00:17:01.311 --> 00:17:02.604
She's not here.

00:17:03.439 --> 00:17:04.523
This way.

00:17:05.482 --> 00:17:07.067
Come this way.

00:17:07.776 --> 00:17:09.820
I won't hurt you.

00:17:11.071 --> 00:17:12.364
Please.

00:17:13.365 --> 00:17:15.034
Get me out of here.

00:17:20.039 --> 00:17:21.999
Thank you.

00:17:23.333 --> 00:17:24.918
<i>What is this machine for?</i>

00:17:25.627 --> 00:17:30.090
<i>I don't know why,</i>
<i>but they keep pumping me full of blood.</i>

00:17:30.674 --> 00:17:34.344
Then they somehow use
my regenerative ability

00:17:34.428 --> 00:17:36.346
to generate electricity.

00:17:37.598 --> 00:17:40.142
You saw the postcard too, didn't you?

00:17:41.185 --> 00:17:44.897
<i>They use that to lure people</i>
<i>who have nowhere else to go.</i>

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:47.733
And they use vampires
like they've used me.

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:50.944
<i>Fine is in danger.</i>

00:17:52.613 --> 00:17:53.822
Hurry! You have to leave!

00:17:57.993 --> 00:18:01.246
If we sacrifice a few people,
everyone else can live peacefully.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:03.082
It's an amazing idea, isn't it?

00:18:03.165 --> 00:18:06.835
This place is the only paradise
on this planet.

00:18:07.628 --> 00:18:08.962
Where is Fine?

00:18:09.046 --> 00:18:10.672
She'll be here soon.

00:18:12.216 --> 00:18:14.384
And she'll replace that man--

00:18:21.016 --> 00:18:23.727
You really do put up a good fight, Momo.

00:18:25.104 --> 00:18:28.857
I still can't believe
people can exist out here.

00:18:29.358 --> 00:18:34.029
This rustic town
runs off of that enormous submarine.

00:18:34.613 --> 00:18:36.532
This'll be interesting.

00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:40.953
You think you've made it this far
without hurting anyone else?

00:18:41.036 --> 00:18:44.414
Don't forget that you arrived here
in blood-soaked clothes.

00:18:44.498 --> 00:18:47.126
Which means you killed someone
at some point, right?

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.336
But it's okay.

00:18:49.837 --> 00:18:53.257
If you beg for forgiveness,
we can put all of this behind us.

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.425
<i>We'll accept you.</i>

00:18:57.136 --> 00:18:59.138
Good evening, travelers.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:03.142
What has brought you
this far into the countryside?

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:06.812
A girl, around 14 years old,
must've come through here.

00:19:06.895 --> 00:19:07.938
Her name's Momo.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:11.900
No one matching that description
has passed through here.

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:15.362
You're wasting your time. Drop the act.

00:19:23.287 --> 00:19:24.705
That's what I'm talking about.

00:19:24.788 --> 00:19:26.456
-Is everyone prepared?
-Yes.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.667
All right, begin the attack.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.503
Kill all invaders!

00:19:32.171 --> 00:19:33.881
It's just like Fine said.

00:19:33.964 --> 00:19:37.426
I was stupid to believe their lies.

00:19:40.554 --> 00:19:42.139
I missed.

00:20:14.004 --> 00:20:16.423
Spill it. Where is Momo?

00:20:17.799 --> 00:20:20.344
She escaped. Into the submarine.

00:20:33.315 --> 00:20:35.901
Looky, I found you.

00:20:35.984 --> 00:20:39.071
What will you do now?
How are you going to scuttle away?

00:20:39.154 --> 00:20:41.657
Maybe you'd like to try calling for help?

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:44.034
Try it. Say, "Fine."

00:20:55.629 --> 00:20:57.506
It's no use trying to run.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.883
You're going to live here.

00:20:59.967 --> 00:21:02.844
You wanted to.
That's why you came here, isn't it?

00:21:02.928 --> 00:21:06.765
We promised
that we'd stay together forever.

00:21:07.808 --> 00:21:09.893
Come on. Say you agree.

00:21:10.477 --> 00:21:12.896
Didn't we say we were officially friends?

00:21:14.064 --> 00:21:16.024
I'll never be friends with you.

00:21:17.359 --> 00:21:19.444
Come on. Be honest with yourself.

00:21:19.987 --> 00:21:22.114
I promise if you do that,

00:21:22.197 --> 00:21:25.117
I'll show you so many more
fun things we can do together.

00:21:30.747 --> 00:21:32.666
I'm sorry to tell you this, Momo.

00:21:33.458 --> 00:21:38.755
You're going to stay here
and be my friend forever.

00:22:00.777 --> 00:22:01.987
Fine.

00:23:53.598 --> 00:23:58.603
Subtitle translation by: Angie Yaeyama
